  <h2>
    How to Make Winter Activewear Look Chic
  </h2>

  <p>
    The easiest way to create a polished workout look is to keep the palette
    simple and focus on layers. Start with a matching base, add one practical
    outer layer and finish with accessories in complementary shades. Textures
    such as ribbed knits, matte leggings and a softly structured jacket can
    make even a simple outfit feel considered.
  </p>

  <div class="style-note">
    Style note: Build around two or three colors you love, then repeat them
    across your leggings, jacket, socks and accessories. Coordinated does not
    have to mean a perfectly matching set.
  </div>

  <p>
    For running outdoors, dress for the conditions and remember that you may
    warm up once you start moving. Layers that are easy to unzip or remove
    are often more comfortable than one very heavy piece. In low light, choose
    visible or reflective details and make sure your footwear suits the route
    and weather.
  </p>

  <p>
    Most importantly, choose pieces that feel good to move in. Stylish
    activewear should support your routine, not complicate it. A few
    well-chosen winter essentials can make getting out the door feel
    that little bit easier.
  </p>

